        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gayla Peevey, John Rox\n- Places: Oklahoma City, Oklahoma\n- Products: \"I Want a Hippopotamus for Christmas\"\n- Topics: Christmas novelty songs, pop charts\n\nFacts:\n- Gayla Rienette Peevey was born on March 8, 1943, and she is a former singer and child star from Oklahoma City, Oklahoma.\n- John Rox wrote the Christmas novelty song \"I Want a Hippopotamus for Christmas.\"\n- In 1953, 10-year-old Gayla Peevey performed \"I Want a Hippopotamus for Christmas.\"\n- In December 1953, \"I Want a Hippopotamus for Christmas\" peaked at number 24 on Billboard magazine's pop chart.",
